Stable FFmpeg media runtime
===========================

Backend development/production and optional go2rtc use a verified FFmpeg 9.0.2
source build against stable Alpine 3.24 libraries. The release tarball is pinned
by SHA-256 and checked using its detached upstream signature and the pinned
public verification key. Compiler tools and development headers stay in the
builder. Runtime dependencies are generated from ELF sonames and installed from
the signed stable repositories. No Alpine edge repository or opaque third-party
runtime executable is used. Distribution FFmpeg packages must not coexist.

The exact upstream source tarball, signature, public verification key, musl V4L2
patch, build recipe, dependency versions and runtime hashes accompany the image
under /usr/share/freesdn-sources/ffmpeg. License texts are under
/usr/share/licenses/ffmpeg. GPL/version3 and x264/x265 are enabled. This is an
inspectable source bundle for this media build, not a declaration that every
transitive dependency has undergone an independent license/security audit.

Compatibility review is required before upgrading operator-defined exec sources.
Compared with Alpine FFmpeg 8.1.2, the selected 9.0.2 build no longer lists the
legacy v308/v408/v410 encoder names or sonic/v308/v408/v410 decoder names; those
implementations are absent from upstream 9.0.2's codec registry. Do not assume
custom commands using these names will continue to work. All previously listed
filters, protocols and hardware-acceleration methods remain available in the
inspected amd64 build; that is capability enumeration, not physical GPU testing.
H.264/HEVC quality presets, source copy and mono 8 kHz AAC have synthetic native
encode/decode coverage. Hardware, RTSP-network and accelerator-driver acceptance
remain separate. Preserve the previously qualified image digests for rollback.

The support boundary remains Linux amd64. An arm64 recipe branch is
not arm64 release acceptance. No stable multi-architecture manifest is authorized
by an amd64 test pass. Every produced image needs fresh SBOM/vulnerability scans,
media/runtime tests, immutable digest binding and release provenance. Upstream
compiler warnings are retained; successful compilation is not a security audit.

The two ffmpeg-build recipe directories are intentionally byte-identical because
backend and optional services use separate Docker build contexts. Change both
copies together, verify the new upstream signature/hash, inspect capability
changes, rebuild every consumer and qualify their actual published artifacts.
